  "_notes": "Relay-mode demo: TX1 just outside Room 1 in the hallway, on the laptop's USB as the relay gateway. Room 1 has RX2 and RX3 on its back wall; RX1 stands at the far end of the hallway, so hallway motion shows as its own tile instead of hiding inside a room. Meters, origin bottom-left of Room 1, polygon vertices counter-clockwise. A door sits on polygon edge `edge` (edge i runs from vertex i to vertex i+1), starting `offset` m from vertex i. crewSlot is a fixed stacking spot for crew markers, not a measured position. Board positions are approximate (about a foot); the hallway outline is approximate. Floor 2 is SIMULATED: 12 rooms with fake receivers fed by hub/evac_sim.py (replayed real CSI), for the evacuation demo.",
